@@ -19,3 +19,20 @@ resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
   index (no leading zeros, no signs), the `-` token, or descending into a primitive or `null`.
 - Only own members resolve (`__proto__`, `constructor`, array `length` etc. do not, unless an own member).
 - The document is never mutated.
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Patch, an array of `add`,
+`remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations, and returns the resulting document as a new value.
+
+```ts
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar" }, [{ op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }]); // { foo: "bar", baz: "qux" }
+```
+
+- Paths and `from` are JSON Pointers (RFC 6901); `-` appends to an array, `""` addresses the whole document.
+- Throws a `TypeError` if the patch is invalid (not an array, an operation that is not an object, a missing
+  or unknown `op`, a missing `path`, `from` or `value`), a `SyntaxError` for an invalid pointer, and an
+  `Error` when an operation fails (missing target, bad array index, `move` into its own child, failed `test`).
+- Atomic: a failing patch has no effect. Neither the document nor the patch is mutated, and the result shares
+  no structure with either.
+- `test` uses JSON equality: member order is irrelevant. `__proto__` is handled as a plain member name.
