+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-applypatch-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch applyPatch (RFC 6902)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`: apply a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) to a JSON document
+and return the result as a new value, without mutating the input. Throw when the patch is invalid or an
+operation fails.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- Six operations: add, remove, replace, move, copy, test (RFC 6902 §4.1-4.6), paths as JSON Pointers (RFC 6901).
+- add: replaces an existing object member; inserts into an array at index 0..length, "-" appends; "" replaces the whole document; parent must exist.
+- remove/replace: target must exist. move: `from` must exist and not be a proper prefix of `path`. copy: `from` must exist.
+- test: deep equality (object member order irrelevant, numbers by value); failure throws.
+- Invalid patch (not an array, operation not an object, missing/unknown `op`, missing `path`/`from`/`value`) throws.
+- Atomic: any failure throws, and the input is never mutated; result does not alias the input or the patch.
+- No prototype pollution via `__proto__`/`constructor` keys.
+- Tests cover the RFC 6902 Appendix A examples and error paths; README updated.
